{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions","id":448123,"title":"Miscellaneous WtF 2e Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-18T13:04:35-07:00","id":448123,"title":"Miscellaneous WtF 2e Questions","content":"Since the time for errata will shortly close, and hopefully we will receive a WtF 2e FAQ, I thought I would start a thread concerning general or more isolated rules and setting inquiries.<br /> <br /> To begin,<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Do lesser supernatural templates that still retain an Integrity stat, such as Ghouls and Proximi, suffer from Lunacy as do regular humans, or are they immune like Wolf-Blooded?<br /> <br /> 2. With the Living Weapon merit (p.107), does each increase in dot rating include the prior dot's advantages (e.g., does Living Weapon 4 permit a Gauru's bite to be both +1L AND have two levels of armor piercing)?<br /> <br /> 3. Are the Supernatural Merits from God Machine Chronicle available to Wolf-Blooded characters and NPC's? <br /> <br /> 4. For the Merit &quot;Favored Form&quot; at 3 dots (p.106), does the exceptional success at three successes apply to just one facet of a Gift, or to all facets of a chosen Gift possessed by the character?<br /> <br /> 5. Are fetishes only available if created as part of a Rite or acquired by role-playing, or are they available (or must be paid for) with Merit dots? <br /> <br /> 6. In addition to spirit negotiation, can talens be created with the Fetish Rite or an altogether different rite? Do they require or are they available with Merit dots. <br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:15:25-07:00","id":448145,"title":"","content":"1. I would rule no, but I don't know if there's direct guidance on that in the book.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm not sure, but I'd say no just because dot 5 completely negates dot 3 of the merit.<br /> <br /> 3. I would say no, since they don't apply to ghouls and ghouls occupy the same area as wolf blooded in my mind.<br /> <br /> 4. I would say it applies to all facets of the gift.<br /> <br /> 5. I haven't seen any mention of being able to start play with fetishes, but I may have missed it.<br /> <br /> 6. Same as above. I think they have to be done in play with the fetish rite. Again, I could be wrong on that one.<br /> <br /> <br /> You're welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:16:22-07:00","id":448148,"title":"","content":"1) GM discression. Previously they were resistant but not immune.<br /> <br /> 2) No.<br /> <br /> 3) At GM discression, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:12:44-07:00","id":448250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions#post448123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Do lesser supernatural templates that still retain an Integrity stat, such as Ghouls and Proximi, suffer from Lunacy as do regular humans, or are they immune like Wolf-Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, crossover concerns like this come down to ST discretion. Personally, I would rule that they are affected by Lunacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions#post448123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. With the Living Weapon merit (p.107), does each increase in dot rating include the prior dot's advantages (e.g., does Living Weapon 4 permit a Gauru's bite to be both +1L AND have two levels of armor piercing)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not clear. I rule yes, but that's probably one for the errata thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions#post448123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Are the Supernatural Merits from God Machine Chronicle available to Wolf-Blooded characters and NPC's?</div> </div> </div> </div>At ST discretion. I allow minor templates to take supernatural merits, but if they gain a major template they lose them (though sanctity of Merits applies).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions#post448123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. For the Merit &amp;quot;Favored Form&amp;quot; at 3 dots (p.106), does the exceptional success at three successes apply to just one facet of a Gift, or to all facets of a chosen Gift possessed by the character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Should apply to all Facets of the chosen gift as far as I know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions#post448123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. Are fetishes only available if created as part of a Rite or acquired by role-playing, or are they available (or must be paid for) with Merit dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not bought with Merit dots. Personally, I treat Fetishes and Talens as having an availability rating (as per the equipment and services rules) equal to their dot rating, though only through particular channels, and the people willing to trade them usually don't care that much about money and would rather barter them for other powerful items or favors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions#post448123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. In addition to spirit negotiation, can talens be created with the Fetish Rite or an altogether different rite? Do they require or are they available with Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same as above, a Talen is effectively just a consumable Fetish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions#post448123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:43:21-07:00","id":448297,"title":"","content":"Mind you, if you <i>do </i>let your players buy fetishes at chargen I'd go with one experience per dot like merits. Helps if you're building more experienced wolves too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T20:20:47-07:00","id":448738,"title":"","content":"I'm looking at ways to get Beats. Having just come from a vampire game, there seemed to be a good amount. Frenzying gets Beats, losing Humanity and the Conditions it generates can get Beats, resisting Humanity loss and the Conditions that generates can get Beats, taking a Bane, and so on.<br /> <br /> There's the usual, shared with Werewolves. Fulfilling an aspiration, resolving a Condition or taking advantage of a Persistent Condition, turning a Failure to a Dramatic Failure, ending a session. The lethal damage one seems like it will be easier to deal with, with the healing. The big one that stands out, outside of some merits, are the Ban Persistent Conditions. A lot of gifts grant Conditions upon Dramatic Failures or Exceptional Successes, too, and Tracking can give you a Condition on either of those.<br /> <br /> But with the way the Harmony section is written up, there's no mention of whether or not moving Harmony offers conditions, outside of aforementioned Ban when you get low. Do you still suffer the standard Breaking Point Conditions? Or is that not part of a werewolf's experience with Harmony?<br /> <br /> tl;dr Do Breaking Points give you Conditions or Beats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-18-2015, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T00:50:27-07:00","id":448909,"title":"","content":"1: Yes<br /> <br /> 2: Yes<br /> <br /> 3: ST discretion, but yes<br /> <br /> 4: No<br /> <br /> 5:Not really. If you start play with experienced characters I would say yes<br /> <br /> 6: -----&quot;-----<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:06:46-07:00","id":449062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions#post448123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Do lesser supernatural templates that still retain an Integrity stat, such as Ghouls and Proximi, suffer from Lunacy as do regular humans, or are they immune like Wolf-Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Up to the Storyteller. I would suspect Ghouls are immune to Lunacy, no idea whether Proximi would be as their 2nd ed rules aren't out yet. Best ask DaveB on the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. With the Living Weapon merit (p.107), does each increase in dot rating include the prior dot's advantages (e.g., does Living Weapon 4 permit a Gauru's bite to be both +1L AND have two levels of armor piercing)? </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that they are cumulative, yes, so a 5-dot Living Weapon has +1L, Armour Piercing 2 and utterly ignores non-magical armour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Are the Supernatural Merits from God Machine Chronicle available to Wolf-Blooded characters and NPC's? </div> </div> </div>Not by default since they aren't in the Werewolf corebook. If you have the GMC book and want to use them, it's up to the Storyteller and group to decide what they're happy with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. For the Merit &quot;Favored Form&quot; at 3 dots (p.106), does the exceptional success at three successes apply to just one facet of a Gift, or to all facets of a chosen Gift possessed by the character? </div> </div> </div>All Facets of the chosen Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Are fetishes only available if created as part of a Rite or acquired by role-playing, or are they available (or must be paid for) with Merit dots? </div> </div> </div>Fetishes are only available if created through the Rite or acquired during the game. They are not bought with Merit dots.<br /> <br /> If you wanted Fetishes to be available at the beginning of the game, I would suggest that you <i>don't</i> map them one-to-one against Merit dots. A 5-dot Fetish holds an <i>immensely</i> powerful spirit within it, with commensurate levels of power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. In addition to spirit negotiation, can talens be created with the Fetish Rite or an altogether different rite? Do they require or are they available with Merit dots. </div> </div> </div>I originally had in mind a seperate Talen Rite but cut it for both space reasons and because it detracted from the main theme of how you get Talens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T06:39:14-07:00","id":449120,"title":"","content":"Thanks again, Chris. <br /> <br /> While you're in the answering mood, I'd thought I'd also inquire about another setting question that I first raised and discussed in the errata thread.<br /> <br /> How and from whom do the Pure receive Renown brands?<br /> <br /> The books states that Renown brands are specifically bestowed by Lunes. However, the Pure do not have a bond with Luna. The Blood Talon Siskur-Dah Condition also indicates Pure have red brands as opposed to the Forsaken's silver. Do Lunes still brand the Pure, is it done by other spirits, and do the Pure have the same ability as the Foresaken to Flare Renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:25:30-07:00","id":449293,"title":"","content":"Ritual scarification. It's essentialy burning red scars upon their corpus. They literally cut the silver out of their flesh over the course of this very painful ritual. It's also how they remove auspice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:33:02-07:00","id":449773,"title":"","content":"Another question. The First Tongue is a spoken language, but there are glyphs and rough runes and symbols involved, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:45:17-07:00","id":449796,"title":"","content":"Yet another question:<br /> <br /> Should Storytellers be concerned about the Action Economy, by this I refer to everyone getting one action per turn, and the issues that crop up when a single Antagonist has only one action, but their are four Player characters, each with their own action.<br /> <br /> Should we be drafting in special Numina or Antagonist rules for single Antagonists to be comparable to a party (or pack) of Player characters or should we let the brutal and fast combat speak for itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:57:25-07:00","id":449800,"title":"","content":"Multiple actions has proven very chaotic in the past with WoD. If the players outnumber their foe then they have the advantage. Ideally that foe should either be beaten by the pack or be something that is so potent that the pack needs to have those extra actions to deal with the secondary problems it creates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T15:06:29-07:00","id":449809,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are all about the advantages of ganging up on something and kicking the shit out of it anyway. Pack Tactics and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T15:10:40-07:00","id":449810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=449796#post449796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we be drafting in special Numina or Antagonist rules for single Antagonists to be comparable to a party (or pack) of Player characters or should we let the brutal and fast combat speak for itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, because you can just add minor opponents. Hosts and spirits tend to have servants, lesser spirits that hang around them and do their bidding. But if you want there's already a few Numina that allow for that sort of thing, like <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+ST+Resources\" target=\"_blank\">Proxy, Spirit Minions, Animal Control and so forth</a>. It outright states that when you're building Claimed, the Dread Powers you use are just up to the Storyteller, so you should be able to see what your players have access to and work from there, whether it's giving them minions or more armor, whatever you need that's thematically appropriate for the beastie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-19-2015, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T20:41:19-07:00","id":450074,"title":"","content":"Yet another question:<br /> <br /> Does a werewofl's resistance to toxin and disease (p. 95) offer any protection from the Toxic Bite and Venomous Ichor Dread Powers and/or the Poisoned and Sick Tilts?<br /> <br /> Also, is the Poison/Toxin Chart from the old NWOD corebook (p.181) still valid under the 2e rules, particularly since both the WtF 2e and GMC rules update fail to provide any suggested disease or toxin levels/penalties.<br /> <br /> Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 03-19-2015, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T23:40:35-07:00","id":450203,"title":"","content":"As written, Poisoned and Sick get around the resistance to toxins and disease. The resistance applies to Toxicity rolls, which neither of those use. Against supernatural powers/Dread Powers, that doesn't bug me. Against mundane sources I'd probably allow a toxin/disease resistance roll on the turn they get hit with something, and use those Tilts for the remainder of combat if they fail the roll.<br /> <br /> The Poison/Toxin chart hasn't been overridden, so I'd say it still applies. The errata to 1e's original roll has been included in the 2e material so far. I'm not seeing a big reason to adjust it. Though I prefer the WOD: Armory expansion of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T04:16:53-07:00","id":450291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=449120#post449120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks again, Chris.<br /> <br /> While you're in the answering mood, I'd thought I'd also inquire about another setting question that I first raised and discussed in the errata thread.<br /> <br /> How and from whom do the Pure receive Renown brands?<br /> <br /> The books states that Renown brands are specifically bestowed by Lunes. However, the Pure do not have a bond with Luna. The Blood Talon Siskur-Dah Condition also indicates Pure have red brands as opposed to the Forsaken's silver. Do Lunes still brand the Pure, is it done by other spirits, and do the Pure have the same ability as the Foresaken to Flare Renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure can flare Renown, yes. They're not branded by Lunes. I can't remember off-hand what they *are* branded by but I would assume either ritemasters or their totems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:06:51-07:00","id":450778,"title":"","content":"Does the bonus from the Wolf Blooded Merit <i>Haikon-Ur's Blood</i> stack with itself if the character is denied multiple senses? For example, would a character who was blindfolded and had their ears plugged receive +4 on perception rolls involving smell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T16:35:57-07:00","id":450990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=449062#post449062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that they are cumulative, yes, so a 5-dot Living Weapon has +1L, Armour Piercing 2 and utterly ignores non-magical armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my understanding as well. Otherwise buying the extra dot can represent a major downgrade when you no longer gain +1L and Armor Piercing 2 against magical armor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T17:32:21-07:00","id":453422,"title":"","content":"So I was reading The Gift of Rage Wisdom Facet Still Small Voice. I'm wondering what's up with the Exceptional success. It claims that upon an Exceptional success the targets then can add the gift users Wisdom renown to their rolls to resist death rage. But there's no roll to resist death rage so I'm confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T22:00:03-07:00","id":453827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Inevitable</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=453422#post453422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was reading The Gift of Rage Wisdom Facet Still Small Voice. I'm wondering what's up with the Exceptional success. It claims that upon an Exceptional success the targets then can add the gift users Wisdom renown to their rolls to resist death rage. But there's no roll to resist death rage so I'm confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves within 10 yards of a packmate in Basu-Im have to roll Resolve + Composure and enter Basu-Im on a failure. I'm pretty sure this is the roll it's talking about. I would also rule that it applies to rolls to gain lucidity in Wasu-Im.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T01:27:34-07:00","id":463204,"title":"","content":"I have a question of my own. Are loci portable? The book lists objects and creatures as possible loci so it sounds like you can move your loci around. If it moves to some place that isn't resonant, should that cause problems? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T04:31:06-07:00","id":463310,"title":"","content":"The locus object itself should be sufficiently resonant, otherwise it wouldn't be a locus. <br /> <br /> The old books talked about portable loci but as a separate thing to the standard. I think what was normally supposed to happen if you moved the focus was that the locus centre would sort of gradually follow it. Personally I'd just have any movable object be a portable locus though. Just seems easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T05:50:18-07:00","id":463372,"title":"","content":"A few questions about werewolves Reaching, taking stuff with them, and combat in the Shadow:<br /> <br /> While in the Shadow, Spirits are automatically &quot;manifested&quot; in that there's no state of Twilight for them to default to anyway, and are effectively &quot;solid&quot;, right?<br /> Can travelers in the Shadow take firearms and other complex devices and expect them to work properly?<br /> Assuming the answer to the first question is &quot;Yes&quot;, does that mean that werewolves can deal damage to Spirits using normal combat rules? So Spirits just roll Power + Finesse - Werewolf defense, and werewolves attack Spirits as normal and whittle away at their Corpus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:02:44-07:00","id":463470,"title":"","content":"Yep, that's pretty much the long and short of it. If I remember right (and the devs didn't change it) when something material enters the shadow it become ephemera itself, so really it's not that they can't default to twilight but rather that the particular state of being defined as &quot;spirit twilight&quot; is the only frequency anything can exist on at all. <br /> <br /> Regardless, yes. Guns still work, Claws function better than ever, party time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:30:53-07:00","id":463512,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this part has changed, but things like cell phones or radios wouldn't work normally, as there's no cell phone towers and cell phone tower spirits wouldn't be compatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:43:52-07:00","id":463533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=463512#post463512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this part has changed, but things like cell phones or radios wouldn't work normally, as there's no cell phone towers and cell phone tower spirits wouldn't be compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A cell phone that works by reaching across the guantlet is a great idea for a Iron Master fetish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:49:31-07:00","id":463559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=463533#post463533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A cell phone that works by reaching across the guantlet is a great idea for a Iron Master fetish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Damn straight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T08:04:51-07:00","id":463566,"title":"","content":"It was. The Lodge of Wires had a sort of bluetooth headset with eye piece that scrolled through news and, presumably, whatever you had programmed it to check on. It maintained contact with the Lodge of Wires' secure networks, and allowed the user to peek through nearby surveillance cameras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:09:27-07:00","id":463604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=463559#post463559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damn straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, when the werewolf receives his cellular bill, the roaming and long-distance charges from using such a fetish would require a successful Resolve + Composure roll, with a -1 to the roll for every dot in Resources below 5, or immediately enter <i>Basu-Im</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:50:02-07:00","id":463622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=463204#post463204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question of my own. Are loci portable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not generally, no. They have physical foci but if you take those away it tends to break the Locus, iirc, until such a time as it resettles on a new focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T10:01:14-07:00","id":463626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=463204#post463204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question of my own. Are loci portable? The book lists objects and creatures as possible loci so it sounds like you can move your loci around. If it moves to some place that isn't resonant, should that cause problems? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well...there is a Wolf-Blooded Tell that effectively makes the character a locus. So...I guess that counts as a portable locus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:12:03-07:00","id":463661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/448123-miscellaneous-wtf-2e-questions?p=463626#post463626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well...there is a Wolf-Blooded Tell that effectively makes the character a locus. So...I guess that counts as a portable locus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't that only in regards to spirits crossing over? Or they generate essence as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/cor